\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S1}{\ignorespaces The spaces the comparison is made in, and what the nominal value is worth once the choices behind it are counted. Red marks the authentic agents, blue the three incumbent simulants and orange the interferents and solvents; only agents and simulants are labelled. (a) Principal components of the structural space and (b) of the three-coordinate GFN2-xTB electronic space, both on the twenty-eight-compound panel, so that the five literature simulants do not appear in them; the leading structural component is a size axis and the leading electronic component loads the two orbital energies against the dipole moment. (c) The mean-difference statistic for 2000 random three-descriptor subspaces of the structural space, before and after ZCA whitening, with the space used here marked: its 0.028 is the 22.4th percentile of those draws, and 28.95\% of them fall below 0.05 as measured, 17.25\% after whitening. (d) Smallest adjusted value over the eighteen tests of each configuration under the six accounting schemes of Table~\ref {tab:family}; on the twenty-eight-compound panel only the scheme that fixes the statistic in advance falls below 0.05, and the fourth configuration falls below it under every scheme. Local reactivity at phosphorus and the rank of the Parr index are in Figure~\ref {fig:plocal}.}}{14}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:spaces}{{S1}{14}{The spaces the comparison is made in, and what the nominal value is worth once the choices behind it are counted. Red marks the authentic agents, blue the three incumbent simulants and orange the interferents and solvents; only agents and simulants are labelled. (a) Principal components of the structural space and (b) of the three-coordinate GFN2-xTB electronic space, both on the twenty-eight-compound panel, so that the five literature simulants do not appear in them; the leading structural component is a size axis and the leading electronic component loads the two orbital energies against the dipole moment. (c) The mean-difference statistic for 2000 random three-descriptor subspaces of the structural space, before and after ZCA whitening, with the space used here marked: its 0.028 is the 22.4th percentile of those draws, and 28.95\% of them fall below 0.05 as measured, 17.25\% after whitening. (d) Smallest adjusted value over the eighteen tests of each configuration under the six accounting schemes of Table~\ref {tab:family}; on the twenty-eight-compound panel only the scheme that fixes the statistic in advance falls below 0.05, and the fourth configuration falls below it under every scheme. Local reactivity at phosphorus and the rank of the Parr index are in Figure~\ref {fig:plocal}}{figure.1}{}}
