\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S8}{\ignorespaces The exact permutation tests over the four panel and designation constructions, by descriptor space and statistic. Values are one-sided $p$. Bold marks $p<0.05$ before correction. The last column is the smallest Benjamini--Hochberg value over the eighteen tests of that panel construction. $^{\dagger }$The volatility axis was specified separately and is not a member of any of those families; the value given for it is the Benjamini--Hochberg minimum over its own six statistics, and Section~\ref {M-res:vol} gives what it becomes under wider families. Dimensions are the retained coordinate counts after the correlation filter of Section~\ref {meth:orderinvariance}; the volatility axis is a single measured quantity and carries no filter. Two further enumerations are reported in the text rather than here, the two-pesticide and acetonitrile relabellings of Section~\ref {M-res:panels} (\texttt  {outputs/twolabel\_panel.json}, \texttt  {outputs/acetonitrile\_panel.json}).}}{26}{table.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:ablation}{{S8}{26}{The exact permutation tests over the four panel and designation constructions, by descriptor space and statistic. Values are one-sided $p$. Bold marks $p<0.05$ before correction. The last column is the smallest Benjamini--Hochberg value over the eighteen tests of that panel construction. $^{\dagger }$The volatility axis was specified separately and is not a member of any of those families; the value given for it is the Benjamini--Hochberg minimum over its own six statistics, and Section~\ref {M-res:vol} gives what it becomes under wider families. Dimensions are the retained coordinate counts after the correlation filter of Section~\ref {meth:orderinvariance}; the volatility axis is a single measured quantity and carries no filter. Two further enumerations are reported in the text rather than here, the two-pesticide and acetonitrile relabellings of Section~\ref {M-res:panels} (\texttt {outputs/twolabel\_panel.json}, \texttt {outputs/acetonitrile\_panel.json})}{table.8}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S9}{\ignorespaces Six ways of accounting for the search, applied to the eighteen tests of each panel configuration. The Westfall-Young min-$P$ value \cite  {westfall1993} is exact for the dependence among the tests, since all eighteen share one enumeration of designations; $m_{\mathrm  {eff}}$ approximates that dependence from the eigenvalues of the correlation matrix of the eighteen nulls \cite  {liji2005}, used as a Bonferroni divisor. On the primary panel no scheme returns anything below 0.05 and on the smaller panel only the pre-specified-statistic scheme does, while the fourth configuration, which differs from the second by two class labels, is below 0.05 under every scheme.}}{26}{table.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:family}{{S9}{26}{Six ways of accounting for the search, applied to the eighteen tests of each panel configuration. The Westfall-Young min-$P$ value \cite {westfall1993} is exact for the dependence among the tests, since all eighteen share one enumeration of designations; $m_{\mathrm {eff}}$ approximates that dependence from the eigenvalues of the correlation matrix of the eighteen nulls \cite {liji2005}, used as a Bonferroni divisor. On the primary panel no scheme returns anything below 0.05 and on the smaller panel only the pre-specified-statistic scheme does, while the fourth configuration, which differs from the second by two class labels, is below 0.05 under every scheme}{table.9}{}}
